## 2. What is SIEM?

**SIEM** stands for **Security Information and Event Management**.

> **🎯 Analyst Analogy:**
> Think of SIEM as a **"CCTV Control Room & Security Guard"** for an enterprise network. Individual devices (servers, routers, laptops) generate log files every time an event happens. SIEM gathers all these clues, analyzes them in real-time, and alerts the security team when an attack occurs.

---

## 3. How SIEM Works

A SIEM solution collects, normalizes, correlates, and visualizes security logs.

```
[ Endpoints / Target VMs ]  ---> (Raw Logs) --->  [ Wazuh Agent ]
                                                          |
                                                          v
[ Wazuh Dashboard (Web UI) ]  <--- (Alerts) <---  [ Wazuh Manager Engine ]

```

### 🔁 The 4-Step SIEM Workflow:

1. **Log Collection:** Wazuh Agents on endpoints continuously collect system & auth logs.
2. **Log Parsing & Normalization:** Converts various log formats into structured JSON data.
3. **Correlation & Detection:** Applies detection rules to identify malicious patterns (e.g., 10 failed SSH logins within 1 minute followed by 1 successful login = Brute Force Attack).
4. **Alerting & Visualization:** Displays alerts on the web dashboard with severity levels.

